# Earthcraft: "Tap an untapped creature you control: Untap target basic land." The cost needs an untapped creature
# you control (CR 602.2): on turn 3 Bot1's only creature, Llanowar Elves, is tapped for mana, so the ability is refused even
# though Bot2 has an untapped Ornithopter (not Bot1's); on turn 5 with the Elves untapped (the positive control) the
# target must be a basic land: Strip Mine, a nonbasic land, is refused, and Bot2's tapped Island - a basic land of
# either player's - is accepted and untaps.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Llanowar Elves
Earthcraft
Strip Mine
Forest
Forest x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Earthcraft.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Strip Mine.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Earthcraft.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Forest)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
! Bot1.Battlefield.Earthcraft.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Strip Mine)
Bot1.Battlefield.Earthcraft.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
